{
  "name": "Resonance Core",
  "icon": "cyberfarm:resonance_core",
  "category": "cyberfarm:energy_storage",
  "sortnum": 2,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "cyberfarm:resonance_core",
      "text": "CyberFarm's big battery, from 1,000,000 FE up to 2,000,000,000 FE: a pedestal with a crystal floating over it, built bigger tier by tier from three blocks.$(br)$(li)$(item)Resonance Core$()$(br)$(li)$(item)Resonance Cell$()"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(li)$(item)Stabilizer Pylon$()"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(li)$(l)Core$(): place the $(item)Resonance Core$(), the pedestal. Alone it is tier 1.$(br)$(li)$(l)Shell$() (tiers 2 to 4): a $(l)hollow cube$() of $(item)Resonance Cell$()s right above the pedestal, centred on it. Every block of its surface is a cell and $(l)the middle block stays empty$(): the crystal grows there, so a",
      "title": "Building it"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(li)3x3x3 takes 26 cells and does not form with a 27th in the middle. To go up a tier, build the next shell round the old one: its cells can stay inside. When the last cell goes in, the cells vanish into the bigger crystal. One craft makes 4 cells.$(br)$(li)$(l)Pylon columns$(): stacks of $(item)Stabilizer Pylon$()s on the $(l)same$()"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(li)$(l)level$() as the pedestal, $(l)in line with it$() on its sides, one per side. A tier needs as many columns as its number, each at least one block taller than the tier, within the distance in the table, with nothing between it and the crystal. A linked column's drone flies up and circles the crystal."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "The $(l:basics/multiblock_projector)Multiblock Projector$(/l) shows tiers 2 to 4, pylons included: sneak + right-click to pick the tier, then click the pedestal."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "At its smallest, with the pylons at their closest. Drag to turn the scene.$(br2)$(l)Tier 1$()$(br2)The core alone: one pylon column, two blocks tall, at least three blocks away.",
      "title": "Every tier"
    },
