    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(li)With enough linked columns the core is $(l)Online$(): the crystal spins, shines white and its heart grows as it fills.$(br)$(li)With too few it is $(l)Unstable$(): the crystal flickers violet and $(l)nothing goes in or out$(), but what it stores is kept.",
      "title": "Online, Unstable and the screen"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Right-click $(l)any part$() to open the screen: the pedestal, any cell (finished shell or not) or any block of a lined-up column. It shows the tier, the columns it has and needs, what it found on each side (a linked pylon, or no pylon, too close, too far, too short, beam blocked) and the FE stored."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Power goes in and out $(l)only through linked pylons$(): connect cables to $(l)any block$() of a column. An $(l:cables/energy_conduit)Energy Conduit$(/l) plugs into a socket on the pylon's side.$(br)$(li)$(l)To fill it$(): cables and generators push into a pylon, CyberFarm's or any other mod's.",
      "title": "Power in and out"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(li)$(l)To draw from it$(): the core never pushes by itself. $(l)Right-click the arm$() of the conduit that touches a pylon so it $(l)pulls$() (see $(l:cables/cables)Cables$(/l))."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(li)$(l)1$(): none, 1,000,000 FE, 1, 2, 3-8, 16,000 FE/t$(br)$(li)$(l)2$(): 3x3x3 (26), 32,000,000 FE, 2, 3, 4-10, 128,000 FE/t$(br)$(li)$(l)3$(): 5x5x5 (98), 256,000,000 FE, 3, 4, 5-12, 512,000 FE/t$(br)$(li)$(l)4$(): 7x7x7 (218), 2,000,000,000 FE, 4, 5, 6-14, 2,000,000 FE/t",
      "title": "Numbers"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Column height is the least a column needs; distance is in blocks from the pedestal."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(li)Breaking a cell drops the core back a tier, and $(l)the energy that no longer fits is lost$(). Empty the core before you rebuild it.$(br)$(li)Breaking the pedestal leaves the cells visible again, but $(l)all the energy stored is lost$().",
      "title": "Tips"
    },
